{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>I would take wing</b> — Know that the western region is called פאת מערב ים (the seaward side) because the Great Sea is to the west of the land of Israel. But אחרית הים (the end of the sea) — the meaning is: actual sea. For he has already mentioned the heavens and the earth, whose depth is Sheol, and now he will mention the sea." "<b>And the meaning of wings of dawn</b> — it is as if he had wings that fly swiftly, to lift and bear him aloft, for at the moment of dawn's rising, light spreads from the eastern edge to the western end — the light seen in the clouds before the sun shines. This too is a weighty interpretation."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 139, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:08.148540116Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}